          "fill": "$text-primary",
          "content": "Relay · Settings, Hermes: no shell on Hermes, Hermes too old, no gateway, a test unanswered, turning it off, and a gateway's own states",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 20,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "sIhqv",
          "name": "intro",
          "fill": "$text-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1100,
          "content": "The switch needs a shell on Hermes's machine, local or over SSH; with a remote URL alone, the commands are shown to run by hand. Before the first step, Tars says what would stop it. A failure at any step names it, says what was put back, and leaves the switch off and the Tars bot on. Once on, each gateway keeps its own state, as Telegram's did in Connection.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
